OpenBark third-party data notices
=================================

This file covers data, not software, that ships inside OpenBark. Software and
model notices are in NOTICE. A copy of this file ships with the app in
licenses/vocabulary-data.txt (apps/desktop/public/licenses/vocabulary-data.txt)
and its text is shown in Settings, About.


Veterinary vocabulary data
--------------------------

OpenBark's drug-name list (packages/vocab/regulatory.tsv, made by
scripts/vocab-import.py; retrieved 28 October 2026) includes names from these
public regulatory datasets, reduced to brand and ingredient words and
deduplicated. Source ids as used in that file are in brackets.

- [us-fda-gb] US Food and Drug Administration, Approved Animal Drug Products
  (Green Book), via Animal Drugs @ FDA
  (https://animaldrugsatfda.fda.gov/). US government work, public domain.

- [uk-vmd] Veterinary Medicines Directorate (UK), Product Information Database
  (https://www.vmd.defra.gov.uk/ProductInformationDatabase/). Contains public
  sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0
  (https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/).

- [ca-dpd] Health Canada, Drug Product Database
  (https://www.canada.ca/en/health-canada/services/drugs-health-products/drug-products/drug-product-database.html).
  Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence - Canada
  (https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada).

- [au-apvma] Australian Pesticides and Veterinary Medicines Authority, PubCRIS
  dataset for registered agricultural and veterinary chemical products
  (data.gov.au), licensed under CC BY 3.0 AU
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/au/). Changed: names extracted.

- [eu-ema] Source: European Medicines Agency (EMA), medicines data
  (https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/download-medicine-data); the names
  of veterinary medicines only.

None of these organisations endorses OpenBark. Brand names are trade marks of
their owners and appear only so speech recognition can catch them.

Everyday English words
----------------------

The list of everyday words that resemble a drug name
(packages/vocab/everyday.tsv) is taken from the SCOWL word lists
(http://wordlist.aspell.net/), which are also used to leave ordinary words out
of the drug-name list. The collective work is Copyright 2000-2018 by Kevin
Atkinson as well as the other copyrights named in its notice, which ships with
the app in licenses/scowl-copyright.txt
(apps/desktop/public/licenses/scowl-copyright.txt).
